  "title": "Ecotone — Full Collection",
  "summary": "<em>An “ecotone” is a region of transition between two biological communities which is richer in species than both.</em><sup>1</sup>\n\nOur exhibition Ecotone distills the creative outflows of the Glitch community of artists and technologists. This growing network considers digital and natural ecologies to be innately entangled, with cross-border collaboration a vital means of generating new social realities. Involving over 60 participants from around the world, Glitch is a spectrum of strategies and a model for a new creator ecology — artistic, poetic, and human-machinic.\n\nFor this show with Feral File, Glitch is represented by leading artists whose diverse approaches reflect the community's plurality. Their works are products of cross-pollination, and non-exhibitors also share their perspectives.\n\nThese contributions illuminate Glitch's ethos: from Yessin Schiegg's view of it as a \"divine force\" in creative completion, to Leonie Schramm's emphasis on \"multi-species connections\" and \"radical and sensual play\" for a \"network of solidarity.\" Tony Lai's \"BioGlitch\" explores \"co-created mechanisms for life and connection\" and \"technoetic awareness\" for all life, including via \"BioGlitch NFTs.\" Vanille Verloës offers a poetic vision of \"L’utopie\" and \"L’Amour\" through collective action.\n\nThis participatory spirit extends to a smart contract for \"glitch collective fill-in hypertext.\" It creates a living, evolving record where users contribute text to 80 blank spaces. Each contribution costs ETH, with the price doubling for subsequent changes to the same space, fostering a dynamic digital artifact.",
